From e2912fca0f90598161e37e1d4742341032ab3201 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:53:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nbt): preserve native scalar values

NBT stores byte strings even when their contents are not valid UTF-8.
Replacing malformed bytes during Java decoding can collapse distinct keys
and make distinct item names compare equal. Retain those bytes through
isolated low surrogates in the internal Java representation, preserve
valid surrogate pairs, and restore the original bytes on output.

Use the lossless codec for little-endian and network-NBT string IO. Keep
their framing and numeric representations intact. Ordinary packet text
continues to use its existing Unicode decoder. Copies and the Java NBT
envelope preserve the retained bytes without a synthetic tag field.

Binary NBT loads float NaNs and non-finite doubles as positive zero, while
preserving float infinities, signed zero and finite bits. Apply those
numeric rules at the binary-NBT stream boundary without mutating source
tags. Generic little-endian and network-NBT numbers keep their behavior.

Evidence targets Bedrock 1.26.51.1, protocol 2193, executable SHA-256
537c0aee2e79afbdc94b44b28e00f466ae62bc50e2733d953b430db9dbaa9ee7.
Complete parsed ItemStack construction142484090/1424a3e70, binary userdata
loader1424d06e0, NBT parser142555580 and comparator14254a410 retain raw keys,
display names and string lists in 340 inputs and 680 directional checks.
Typed registries, virtual interfaces and runtime/allocator hosting remain
supplied boundaries; this is not full packet decoding or native pixels.

The numeric loader and writer slices14254b9f0/14254b2e0 agree on all 28
scalar bit patterns. The writer probe stops before abstract output
dispatch and does not establish full native packet serialization.

Tests cover distinct malformed keys/names, nested lists, Java NBT transit,
every byte pair, every Unicode scalar and mixed malformed inputs. Each
restored old stream, or broken surrogate-pair handling, fails its relevant
behavioral regression. Native comparisons remain separate from complete
live malformed-NBT inventory acceptance and the unfinished search UI.
